# Daisy Plan Workflow

When `PLAN.md` exists at the workspace root, it is an active Daisy implementation plan: a symlink into the bound home's `plans/` (through `.daisy/plans/`), gitignored. Edit its real path, which `daisy files` prints as `current plan`, never through the link.

Before any plan work, read `.daisy/AGENTS.md` and, in full, the plan workflow prompt it names (`prompts/plan.md`, or the home's override of it where `.daisy/AGENTS.md` points), and follow its rules; this rule does not restate them. In Cursor Plan mode, edit `PLAN.md` only (its rule 2); to execute a plan, follow its rules 20–25.

**To archive a completed plan:**
Run `daisy plan archive` or say `/daisy archive PLAN.md`.
This moves the plan file to `.daisy/plans/archive/` and removes the `PLAN.md` symlink.
